@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{gptel-extras.el} extends @samp{gptel}@comma{} the Emacs package that integrates various Large Language Models---ChatGPT@comma{} Gemini@comma{} Claude@comma{} Perplexity@comma{} local models@comma{} and others---into Emacs buffers. While @samp{gptel} provides the core infrastructure for sending prompts and receiving responses@comma{} @samp{gptel-extras.el} adds workflows and conveniences that make day-to-day use more productive.

The package depends on @samp{gptel} (version 0.7.1 or later)@comma{} @samp{paths} (for directory path resolution) and @samp{simple-extras}.

The extensions fall into several thematic areas:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Aider-style context management.} Commands for generating a repository map (via the external @samp{aider} tool)@comma{} caching it with configurable time-to-live and git-aware invalidation@comma{} and automatically injecting both the map and a project conventions file into the @samp{gptel} context before each request (@ref{Aider context management, , Aider context management}).

@item
@strong{Conversation management.} Automatic saving of new @samp{gptel} buffers to a dedicated directory@comma{} continuation of conversations across linked buffers@comma{} and a workaround for unresponsive @samp{gptel} sessions (@ref{Conversation management, , Conversation management}).

@item
@strong{ChatGPT import.} Bulk import of conversations exported from ChatGPT into Org files (@ref{ChatGPT import, , ChatGPT import}).

@item
@strong{Commit summarization.} Sending selected commit diffs from a Magit log buffer to an LLM for changelog-style summaries (@ref{Commit summarization, , Commit summarization}).

@item
@strong{Search integration.} A command that simultaneously opens a web search and queries a configured AI model (e.g.@comma{} Perplexity Sonar) with the same query (@ref{Search integration, , Search integration}).

@item
@strong{Email drafting.} Integration with @samp{mu4e} and @samp{org-msg} for LLM-assisted email reply drafting (@ref{Email drafting with mu4e, , Email drafting with mu4e}).

@item
@strong{Gptel tools.} A collection of tools---filesystem editing@comma{} bibliography search@comma{} and entry addition---that @samp{gptel} can invoke via its tool-use feature@comma{} plus a macro for defining tool presets (@ref{Tools, , Tools}).

@item
@strong{Automatic model discovery.} Track the newest Claude Opus@comma{} Sonnet@comma{} and Haiku releases and update configured model settings (@ref{Automatic Claude model discovery, , Automatic Claude model discovery}).

@item
@strong{Model-specific workarounds.} Automatic Mullvad VPN activation for Gemini requests and a command for fixing garbled characters in LLM output (@ref{Model-specific workarounds, , Model-specific workarounds}).

@item
@strong{General convenience commands.} Toggling default major mode@comma{} navigating to the end of a buffer before sending@comma{} rewriting function definitions via Embark@comma{} and more (@ref{General convenience commands, , General convenience commands}).
@end itemize

