@node Aider context options
@section Aider context options

@vindex gptel-extras-add-repo-map-to-context
The user option @code{gptel-extras-add-repo-map-to-context} controls whether the repository map is automatically added to the @samp{gptel} context before every request sent via @code{gptel-send}. When non-nil@comma{} the function @code{gptel-extras-add-context-files} generates (or retrieves from cache) the repository map and injects it into the context (@ref{Automatic context injection, , Automatic context injection}).

The default value is @code{nil}. Enable this option when you are using @samp{gptel} for coding tasks within a project and want the LLM to have an overview of the codebase structure@comma{} similar to Aider's built-in repo map feature.

This is a boolean option.

@vindex gptel-extras-add-conventions-to-context
The user option @code{gptel-extras-add-conventions-to-context} controls whether a @samp{conventions.md} file from the project root is automatically added to the @samp{gptel} context before every request. When non-nil@comma{} @code{gptel-extras-add-context-files} calls @code{gptel-extras-add-conventions-to-context} to include this file (@ref{Automatic context injection, , Automatic context injection}).

The default value is @code{nil}. Enable this option if your project has a @samp{conventions.md} file documenting coding standards and you want the LLM to respect them.

This is a boolean option.

@vindex gptel-extras-repo-map-cache-ttl
The user option @code{gptel-extras-repo-map-cache-ttl} specifies the time-to-live for cached repository maps@comma{} in seconds. After this duration@comma{} the cached map is considered stale and will be regenerated on the next request.

The default value is @code{3600} (one hour). Increase this value for large@comma{} stable repositories where the structure rarely changes; decrease it for rapidly evolving codebases.

This is an integer option.

@vindex gptel-extras-repo-map-invalidate-on-git-changes
The user option @code{gptel-extras-repo-map-invalidate-on-git-changes} controls whether the repository map cache is invalidated when the git HEAD reference changes@comma{} regardless of the TTL@. When non-nil@comma{} any new commit@comma{} branch switch@comma{} or rebase that alters HEAD triggers regeneration of the map.

The default value is @code{t}. Disable this option only if you want the map to persist strictly based on the TTL@comma{} ignoring git activity.

This is a boolean option.

@node Email drafting options
@section Email drafting options

@vindex gptel-extras-mu4e-draft-reply-prompt
The user option @code{gptel-extras-mu4e-draft-reply-prompt} specifies the prompt sent to the LLM when drafting an email reply with @code{gptel-extras-mu4e-draft-reply} (@ref{Email drafting with mu4e, , Email drafting with mu4e}). The prompt instructs the model to draft a message based on the attached email thread@comma{} complete any partial draft already present@comma{} and produce only the body text (no headers or signature).

The default value includes the user's full name (from @code{user-full-name}) to help the LLM identify the sender. Customize this option to adjust the drafting instructions@comma{} tone@comma{} or language.

This is a string option.

@node Search options
@section Search options

@vindex gptel-extras-search-model
The user option @code{gptel-extras-search-model} specifies the backend and model to use for the AI component of @code{gptel-extras-search-and-ask-model} (@ref{Search integration, , Search integration}). The value is a cons cell of the form @samp{(BACKEND . MODEL)}@comma{} where @samp{BACKEND} is a string naming a @samp{gptel} backend and @samp{MODEL} is a symbol identifying the model.

The default value is @samp{("Perplexity" . sonar)}. Change this option if you prefer a different search-oriented model or if the Perplexity backend is not configured.

@vindex gptel-extras-search-prefix
The user option @code{gptel-extras-search-prefix} specifies the URL prefix for the web search opened by @code{gptel-extras-search-and-ask-model}. The query string is appended (URL-encoded) to this prefix.

The default value is @samp{"https://www.google.com/search?q}"=. Change this to use a different search engine (e.g.@comma{} DuckDuckGo@comma{} Bing).

This is a string option.

@node Gemini and VPN options
@section Gemini and VPN options

@vindex gptel-extras-gemini-mullvad-disconnect-after
The user option @code{gptel-extras-gemini-mullvad-disconnect-after} specifies the number of minutes after which the Mullvad VPN connection@comma{} activated for a Gemini request@comma{} is automatically disconnected (@ref{Model-specific workarounds, , Model-specific workarounds}).

The default value is @code{1}. Increase this if your Gemini requests take longer than one minute to complete.

This is an integer option.

@node Directory options
@section Directory options

@vindex gptel-extras-dir
The user option @code{gptel-extras-dir} specifies the directory where @samp{gptel} conversation buffers are automatically saved by @code{gptel-extras-save-buffer} (@ref{Saving buffers, , Saving buffers}). The directory is sorted chronologically via a @samp{.dir-locals.el} file@comma{} since the typical use case is to locate a recently modified conversation.

The default value is derived from @code{paths-dir-notes} with @samp{gptel/} appended. Change this if you store your notes elsewhere.

This is a directory option.

@vindex gptel-extras-chatgpt-import-dir
The user option @code{gptel-extras-chatgpt-import-dir} specifies the directory where imported ChatGPT conversations are saved by @code{gptel-extras-import-chatgpt-conversations} (@ref{ChatGPT import, , ChatGPT import}).

The default value is derived from @code{paths-dir-notes} with @samp{chatgpt/} appended.

This is a directory option.

@node Alert options
@section Alert options

@vindex gptel-extras-alert-when-finished
The user option @code{gptel-extras-alert-when-finished} controls whether an alert is displayed after @samp{gptel} finishes inserting a response. It accepts three types of values:

@itemize
@item
@code{t}: always display an alert.
@item
@code{nil}: never display an alert.
@item
A list of model symbols (e.g.@comma{} @code{(gemini-pro claude-opus-4-6)}): display an alert only when the response comes from one of the listed models.
@end itemize

The default value is @code{nil}. This is useful when using slow models where you might switch to another task while waiting for the response. The alert relies on the @samp{alert} package.

